WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.520
Yakitate!! 9, the third match.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.940
Showdown in Saito.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:05.020
The item of importance is...

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:06.940
Ooo, mango!

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.190
CMAP’s special curry bread.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:10.280
All done.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.950
This animal inhabits an area from Myanmar to Thailand, as well as the Malaysian peninsula.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:21.080
A mammal and an odd-toed ungulate,
popularly known as the Malay tapir!

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:21.880
Malay tapir?!

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:24.330
Try saying “Malay tapir” ten times in a row.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.510
Say it quickly.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:32.510
Malay tapir.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.680
And... what was the bread that I just ate?

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:35.760
Malay tapir!

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.230
It’s curry bread!

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:42.270
All right.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:43.690
It’s done!

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:48.570
Th-This is...

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.190
It’s like a haniwa!

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.690
The judge has frozen stiff!

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:56.910
The victor is... Pantasia!

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.410
All right!

00:00:58.910 --> 00:00:59.700
Listen up!

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.870
What your bread completely lacked was...

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:04.370
love.

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:06.000
L-Love?!

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.540
That’s right, love.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:09.500
It was...

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.930
for the sake of love.

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:14.300
The love that the locals put into raising their mangoes,

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.310
and the love that went into wanting to make the local souvenirs more appealing...

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:21.470
That is what made this a great bread!

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:24.930
Love is what’ll save Saito!

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:30.400
Kazuma’s Haniwa-<i>Japan</i> crushed
their fearsome opponent, CMAP.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.350
Having spectacularly won the third round,

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:36.780
Kazuma and the folks from Pantasia were now to face a new battle.

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:43.410
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.330
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.630
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:51.000
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:56.220
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:00.600
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:10.570
I want this voice to reach you, even though it’s still a tiny song.

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:16.740
That’s because I have the feeling that something’s gonna start.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:31.880
As I was cowering, muffling my voice, the tears that I shed

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:40.430
probably helped me notice that

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:46.350
I’ve almost forgotten how to believe.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:55.200
The future that I painted (I will fulfill it)

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.610
Looking up to the clear skies,

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:07.710
I begin to run once again. Someday, I want to dye

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:13.550
that white sky with my colors.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:20.550
I’m going to fly as far as possible, shining like a marble,

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:24.890
unfolding these wings of mine.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:33.480
Nin... Nin... Nin!!

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:36.030
This is my way of the ninja!

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.450
Very well, then.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:46.500
We will now choose the locale for the fourth round of Yakitate!! 9.

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:50.830
All competitors may now enter!

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.670
N-Ninjas?

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:02.680
What was that?!

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:04.180
Cool!

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:07.190
We’ve had popular entertainment stars and assassins...

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:09.560
but now, ninjas?

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:12.070
What the hell does St. Pierre have in mind?

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:14.360
It’s the Surprise Breads from All Around the World Show!

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:15.070
Not quite...

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:17.860
Our opponents are bakers, after all.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.740
Well then, ninjas...
you may select a panel!

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:34.540
Very well. Let’s flip the panel, then!

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:35.500
Oomagari

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.710
Looks like it’s Oomagari.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:40.180
Oomagari
Oomagari refers to Oomagari, in
the city of Daisen in Akita prefecture.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:43.680
Oomagari refers to Oomagari, in
the city of Daisen in Akita prefecture.

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:47.810
Its name is supposed to have been derived from the Omono River that used to wind through it.

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:50.940
It’s famous for things that are curved, such as bent houses.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:53.730
In any case, it’s a city that likes its stuff twisted.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:56.230
If you talk about curves, they
tend to have a bad image to them...

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:59.440
But in any battle, it’s hard to win by only playing straight.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:04.000
We’ll be looking forward to great ideas that
demonstrate the merits of all things that are bent.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:06.000
That is all.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:09.330
Akita prefecture     Oomagari

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.950
We’re here!
Akita prefecture     Oomagari

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:12.420
That was quick.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:14.170
We’re here already.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:19.880
Oomagari hosts a big fireworks festival every year
in August that over 500,000 people come to attend.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:22.970
That’s probably why you can take a direct bullet train from the heart of the city.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.390
500,000? That’s a lot.

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:28.770
But, we can’t eat fireworks.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.970
So what specialty products
are we going to use this time?

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:33.490
Well, you see...

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.190
What was that?!

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:37.850
There are no specialty products in Oomagari?!

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:41.490
No, there are various specialty products.

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:45.660
But Kuroyanagi-senpai emphasized over and over that we should use something bent...

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:49.040
So, don’t you think that we
should use things that are bent?

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:50.830
Now that you mention it...

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:54.750
But are there any bent specialty products
available for our convenience just like that?

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.070
Yep, there are.

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:58.760
At a place a little away from here.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:00.090
At Oota city.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.840
Oota City

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:04.930
Say, Kanmuri...

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:07.430
What kind of bent thing is available in this city?

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:10.100
Well, I don’t want to spoil the surprise,
so let’s wait till we get there.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:13.350
Well, either way, this means that we’ve won for sure.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:15.060
Why?

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:19.900
The only reason we found Oota city
was because of you, Kanmuri.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:24.190
But those weird ninjas in fancy dress
couldn’t possibly know about this place.

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:25.900
I wonder about that...

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:31.160
Th-The ninjas are here, too...?

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:34.910
A mere ninja has...?

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.460
Well, do you understand now, Kawachi-san?

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:41.720
Regardless of what they wear,
they’re artisans hired by St. Pierre.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:43.680
We can’t let our guard down.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:45.340
Doesn’t it bother you?

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:49.680
Why would that good an artisan... cover his face?!

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.390
Doesn’t it bother you guys?!

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:52.270
Nope.

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:53.270
Not really.

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:58.690
It doesn’t matter who they are, all I have
to do is make <i>Japan</i> with everything I have.

00:06:58.690 --> 00:06:59.770
That’s right.

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:02.150
Everybody has their own reasons.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:04.860
It’s a matter of etiquette to
not pry into every little thing.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.400
You have a just argument.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:10.870
But, I... I...

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:14.620
I can’t hold it in anymore!

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:17.750
I’m going to take those masks of yours off!

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:24.930
Wh-What’s that?

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:26.640
That spring onion looks all bent.

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:28.300
It <i>is</i> bent!

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:31.140
Because that is the ingredient
that we were searching for.

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:32.720
It’s bent spring onion!

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:34.610
Bent spring onion?

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:38.860
Oomagari Shuriken,

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:41.030
Spring Onion Windmill!

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:47.030
Kawachi!
Kawachi-san!

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.920
Wh-What the hell is this?

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:58.000
He’s strong.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:01.840
I’ve never fought anyone like this ever before.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:04.010
There you are!

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:10.060
K-Kawarimi no jutsu?!

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.180
This is Oota city,

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:14.220
also known as the village of bent spring onion.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:18.600
It is an area that cultivates a variety of bent spring onion called Yokosawa spring onion.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:20.470
Bent spring onion?

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:25.530
Fire skill: Fried Spring Onion Technique!

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:38.620
Especially soft, and with an exquisite sweetness.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:41.450
The palatability and fragrance of this bent spring
onion, combined with the high-class twist...

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.210
It can’t be possible that you’ve failed to notice this.

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:47.970
You didn’t know about it?

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:50.420
So, what about it?!

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:52.050
In that case, just die!

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:53.690
You don’t have the right to live!

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:55.900
D-Damn it!

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:58.390
Guys...

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.400
Wh-Whatever.

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:07.690
I won’t take back the words I’ve said!

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:10.320
That is the way of my bread!

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:11.870
Interesting.

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:13.490
In that case, I shall explain it to you,

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:15.780
just how awesome the bent bit of this spring onion is.

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:19.170
Spring Onion Cloning Technique!

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:24.090
Spring onion cloning?

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:25.820
Unlike regular cloning,

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:29.130
this is a super-high-level ninja technique,
where every onion has a solid body.

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:30.670
Come on, let’s go!

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:35.630
Yo! Ko! Sa! Wa!

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:36.560
Yo! Ko! Sa! Wa!

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:37.180
Yo! Ko! Sa! Wa!

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:38.430
Yo! Ko! Sa! Wa!

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:45.660
Bent spring onion consecutive strikes.

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:54.610
Watch carefully.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:56.120
Easy for you to say.

00:09:56.580 --> 00:10:01.410
Since bent spring onion is extremely soft, it can’t grow straight up.

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.500
Therefore, after they’ve grown a little,

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:08.380
they’re replanted by laying them in the soil and allowing them to grow again.

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:09.630
When you do that...

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:13.230
They grow toward the light and get bent.

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:17.510
You’re not hurt, are you, Mr. Scaredy Cat?

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:25.490
This is really good spring onion.

00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:31.530
Being bent is...

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:36.820
Wo-n-der-ful!

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:40.750
I got distracted by your technique and didn’t notice,

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:43.700
but now that I look, aren’t you Suwabara?!

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:47.130
Oh, no!

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:48.710
When I did the fire skill technique, I...

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:49.500
Kai!

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.040
Suwabara!
Suwabara-san!

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:06.350
Oh, no!

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:08.610
To think that my identity
was revealed in such a manner...

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:11.110
If Azuma and gang are disturbed by this,

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:13.060
then everything will have been for nothing.

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:14.770
Suwabara?

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:19.280
No, it’s too early to give up.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:24.320
I compliment you on noticing...

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:25.740
is what I’d like to say.

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:29.370
But, I’m not your friend, Suwabara Kai.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:30.800
Huh?

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:32.950
My name is Gai.

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:36.250
I’m his twin brother, Suwabara Gai!

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.210
What was that?!

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:41.800
It looks like you are on good terms with my brother,

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:43.270
but I’m not my brother.

00:11:43.670 --> 00:11:46.270
I’d like it if we could get along as well.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.260
Y-You know...

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:51.260
If you were going to make up an excuse, you really should’ve come up with a better one.

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:53.640
Pleased to meet you, I’m Azuma.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:55.780
Same here. I’m Kanmuri.

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:57.310
Wait a moment!

00:11:57.310 --> 00:11:58.780
What’re you guys doing?

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:00.020
What do you mean?

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:01.610
We’re greeting each other.

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:04.280
I hate to sound repetitious, but my name is Gai.

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:05.450
Suwabara Gai.

00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:08.780
Therefore, there is no reason to hold back in this battle.

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:09.450
Got it?

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:14.330
Farewell!

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:20.000
Well then, let’s get some spring...

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.040
Hey, guys...

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:22.220
Don’t tell me that you two...

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:26.220
actually believe that he was Suwabara’s twin?

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:27.970
Of course not.

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:31.150
That ninja was Suwabara Kai,

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:33.980
and the female ninja was
St. Pierre’s Monica-san, without a doubt.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:35.720
If so, then why?!

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:38.440
In the end, they betrayed us!

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:40.700
Wasn’t it necessary to know the reason for that?

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:42.900
What would you do by knowing it?

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:43.940
What do you mean?

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:46.400
He is a man in search of the ultimate truth.

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:49.780
In order to excel at the way of bread, he’d do anything.

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:53.530
No matter who the victims may be,
he wants to fight with strong people.

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:55.120
Isn’t he that kind of person?

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.870
Then... Then he’s all right with it?

00:12:57.870 --> 00:13:01.830
You mean that he doesn’t care what
happens to his friends... and to Pantasia?

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:04.000
Of course not!

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:06.340
It’s not like Suwabara doesn’t care.

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:07.800
Azuma...

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:08.680
But...

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:15.310
He has something that makes it
worth throwing everything else away for.

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:16.690
That’s all that it is.

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:21.940
In the past, when I was in the
newcomers’ battle with you, Kawachi...

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:27.450
I couldn’t really understand your
feeling of wanting to win against me.

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:29.400
For winning against you.

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:30.620
To win against me?

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:33.030
I’ll win!

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:35.160
I will not lose to you, even if I die.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:36.620
Remember that well.

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:37.550
Kawachi.

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.250
But, now I can understand it.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:43.210
It’s by getting serious about
fighting against strong opponents

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:47.250
that I was able to get closer
and closer to the true <i>Japan</i>.

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:49.720
So, let’s try and understand him.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:52.630
If he’s going to throw everything away to come at us,

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:55.260
we’d be lacking as men if we didn’t take him seriously.

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:56.230
Right, Kawachi?

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:57.640
That’s right.

00:13:57.640 --> 00:13:59.230
That’s what Suwabara-san said.

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:01.480
“There is no reason to hold back.”

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:06.490
That might be true...

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:15.570
I’m sorry, guys...

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:18.920
But, this is the answer that I have arrived at.

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:22.710
That day, shortly after the end of the Monaco Cup,

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:26.970
I met up with my sword master after a long time.

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:29.920
Champions at a world tournament, huh?

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:31.510
Very impressive.

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:32.970
What a joke.

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:36.010
The only reason we won that tournament
was because Azuma was there.

00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:38.440
I was nothing more than decoration.

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:41.390
Is that so?

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:45.450
Well then, you must have a match against
Azuma-kun to vindicate your honor sometime soon.

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:47.730
That is not possible.

00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:52.620
The Yakitate!! 9 show is a fight between Pantasia and St. Pierre.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:55.950
Being on the same side, I cannot fight him.

00:14:57.820 --> 00:14:59.410
Say, Kai...

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:02.210
How about a bit of a sparring match tomorrow?

00:15:03.330 --> 00:15:06.420
We will begin at exactly 6 in the morning.

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:07.670
All right?

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:14.760
Geez.

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:17.810
What can Master be thinking of?

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:22.060
While he may be master swordsman of
the Secret Arts of the Shingou Style...

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:24.270
he couldn’t possibly win against me at his age.

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:25.650
An opening!

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:29.980
M-Master!

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:31.610
How cowardly to strike when I don’t expect it!

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:33.280
You fool!

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:36.990
I told you that the match
would start at exactly 6 o’clock.

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:40.170
It’s your fault for spacing out.

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:44.870
In that case, I won’t hold back.

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:46.630
That’s how it should be, brat.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:03.060
Master! Why did you do this?!

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:05.100
To go so far as to do something cowardly like that...

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:06.430
What were you trying to prove by...?

00:16:06.430 --> 00:16:07.820
That’s right!

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:11.110
I wanted to win against you even if it meant dying!

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:12.540
No matter what I had to do!

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:16.190
Forgetting the will to win, just aging and then dying.

00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:18.780
I don’t wish to live like that!

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:23.540
I don’t wish for my... my student to live like...

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:26.540
I can’t let my student live like that.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:27.790
Master.

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:32.630
Kai. This is the last lesson I give you.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.260
Everyone dies someday.

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:42.230
If you’ve decided to excel at a path,
live every day with the resolve to die for it.

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:47.020
M... Master!

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:51.480
My master died in order to teach me
the way of the true seeker of truth.

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:52.150
Age of retirement: 124 years
My master died in order to teach me
the way of the true seeker of truth.

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:54.490
Age of retirement: 124 years

00:16:56.490 --> 00:17:01.250
He opened my eyes when I was about to
get carried away with the idea of friendship.

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:03.280
Azuma!

00:17:03.280 --> 00:17:05.660
I cannot win against you when it comes to talent,

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:07.790
though our passion is evenly matched.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.080
Therefore, I’ll lay my life on the line.

00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:13.000
I will throw everything away,
and push myself to the edge.

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:15.510
I will release all my power in order to challenge you.

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:20.020
If I lose this battle, I will slash my stomach!

00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:22.850
M-Monica!

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:25.680
H-Hey, Kai...

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:28.270
When you say slash your stomach,
do you mean commit suicide?

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:29.310
Yes.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:32.020
But, you just mean that you’re ready to do it.

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:34.440
You’re not actually gonna do it, right?

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:35.110
I’ll do it.

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:39.440
Since you’re German,
you may not know this.

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:42.290
All Japanese men are like this.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:42.540
<b>Not quite
All Japanese men are like this.</b>

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:44.120
<b>Not quite</b>

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:46.420
I-Is that so...?

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:49.880
But, I don’t want you to die!

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.380
I don’t really want to die yet, either.

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:56.460
That’s why I must win.

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:57.590
That’s all there is to it.

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:02.100
I won’t let you die.

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:05.270
I’ll make sure that you don’t die!

00:18:06.010 --> 00:18:06.980
Monica...?

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:09.220
Definitely...

00:18:09.220 --> 00:18:11.180
We’ll definitely win!

00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:12.400
Okay.

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:16.740
Magari Lodge

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:18.280
Well, then...

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:24.000
We know that our opponent will be using the same ingredients... that is, bent spring onions.

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:26.530
What the hell is with this lodge?

00:18:26.530 --> 00:18:27.990
It’s called Magarisou...

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:29.740
But it’s already bent!

00:18:29.740 --> 00:18:34.580
If we sleep over at such a place, our
organ of balance will go wacko on us.

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:37.500
If happens every time, so I
was beginning to get used to it...

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:41.050
But can’t we do something about
how Kanmuri chooses our lodgings?

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:42.630
Hey, Kawachi-san...

00:18:42.630 --> 00:18:43.770
Are you listening?

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:49.850
If we’re talking about spring onion bread,
you see them at various bakeries.

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:52.400
But their methods of preparation
aren’t really that different.

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:54.900
If you put spring onion into bread,

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:59.900
you’d first dice it, then soak in water and either
boil or stir-fry it before adding to the dough.

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:02.870
I get the feeling that there really is no way to prepare it

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:05.660
other than figuring out how to season it...

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:07.370
No, there is.

00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:09.370
We’ll put it in raw.

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:13.620
You’re going to put the onion in raw?

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:15.540
We’re going up against Azuma and gang.

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:19.420
Only after doing this will we have
the slightest possibility of winning.

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:21.840
That may be true, but...

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:23.920
When you boil spring onion, it turns sweet.

00:19:23.920 --> 00:19:26.140
This has been proven scientifically.

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:31.140
But, when you do that, the spring onion’s
original flavor is lost, and you lose its crispiness.

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:32.770
If you add it to bread,

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:36.940
it’s sure to be more delicious if you add
it to the dough raw and bake it like that.

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:39.650
It is similar in concept to the Korean dish chijimi,

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.150
especially spring onion chijimi.

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:45.570
All you do for that is add raw
onion to the dough and bake it.

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:48.170
The principle doesn’t change,
even when applying it to bread.

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:49.700
In that case...

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:52.670
Why don’t they do it at regular bakeries?

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:55.540
Because you have to knead the bread for a long time.

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:57.790
If you did that, the onion inside would get crushed,

00:19:57.790 --> 00:19:59.920
and then it wouldn’t be any different from boiled onion.

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:02.190
What if you were to knead it
softly so that it doesn’t break?

00:20:02.190 --> 00:20:05.760
In that case, you have “unmixing,”

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:08.090
which is a phenomenon that often occurs when you mix in things like raisins.

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:10.190
It leaves the bread unable to expand.

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:14.180
In short, it’s hard to do and so nobody bothers.

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:18.440
But, this spring onion is bent, and is much softer than the regular stuff.

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:20.860
It won’t crush easily, even when kneaded in.

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:22.900
In addition, we’ll use egg yolk.

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:24.360
Egg yolk?

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:27.030
Here, we have the former queen of the patisserie world.

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:28.610
We have you.

00:20:28.610 --> 00:20:30.820
We’ll have you make it.

00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:33.790
With these famous Akita prefecture
Hinai chicken egg yolks,

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:36.120
we’ll have you make the ultimate blanchir.

00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:37.500
What was that?!

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:39.670
You’re going to use egg yolk?

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:40.630
That’s right.

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:41.790
I see!

00:20:41.790 --> 00:20:46.800
You’ll beat the egg yolks to make blanchir
to keep the bread from getting heavy.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:49.470
Here in Akita, we’ll be able to get
Hinai chicken eggs, so that’s good!

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:51.810
Blanchir?

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:53.350
Um...

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:55.520
If you beat egg whites, you get meringue.

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:58.230
When you beat egg yolk, you get blanchir.

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:01.780
It’s usually used to make cakes fluffy.

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:03.360
Oh, that’s right.

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:04.110
That’s it.

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:05.030
That’s the thing.

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:11.370
This is what you’ve come up with to
make sure that the bread rises, right?

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:14.580
Yeah, that’s pretty much it.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:17.620
Just like Azuma! You’re a genius!

00:21:17.620 --> 00:21:19.040
Is that so?

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:20.290
That’s right!

00:21:20.290 --> 00:21:22.670
The spring onion and egg should go well together.

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:24.510
It really is a genius of an idea!

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:28.430
With this, we won’t lose to that traitor.

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:31.510
But, you know...

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:35.150
I get the feeling that we’re still missing something.

00:21:36.010 --> 00:21:37.770
That’s amazing, Kai!

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:40.810
Even Azuma wouldn’t have
come up with something like this!

00:21:40.810 --> 00:21:42.980
We’re sure to win now!

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:44.740
No, not quite yet.

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:48.860
He’s sure to come up with this level of an idea...

00:21:48.860 --> 00:21:51.960
The question is whether we
take one step further from here.

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:54.580
It’s the something-or-other <i>Japan</i>!

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:58.500
In the “something-or-other” part,
he usually brings in an awesome trick.

00:21:58.500 --> 00:22:02.080
We cannot forget that we have a
fearsome fellow as our opponent.

00:22:02.080 --> 00:22:06.040
That’s why we try and take one step further this time.

00:22:06.040 --> 00:22:08.800
Well, I understand your feelings, but...

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:11.340
do you have an item to surpass these?

00:22:11.340 --> 00:22:12.220
I do!

00:22:12.980 --> 00:22:15.640
I will steal the show from the something-or-other <i>Japan</i>.

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:17.850
Or rather, the Oomagari <i>Lupan</i>...

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:21.520
The Spring Onion Spiral <i>Lupan</i> will!

00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:23.270
Just wait, Azuma,

00:22:23.270 --> 00:22:28.030
and watch with your own eyes the hidden power
of a samurai who has laid his life on the line.

00:22:53.930 --> 00:23:02.230
The world will probably go on today, with a repetition of the same faces,

00:23:02.230 --> 00:23:10.280
but there was one thing that I’d forgotten.

00:23:10.700 --> 00:23:15.050
If I’m to take a deep breath,

00:23:15.050 --> 00:23:19.040
then the shape of the love that permeates my surroundings

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:26.630
will shine so much that it’s blinding.

00:23:27.010 --> 00:23:35.010
Someone is calling me from far away...

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:43.400
And that voice constantly echoes in my heart.

00:23:43.610 --> 00:23:51.990
So, riding on my small pleasures, the merry-go-round begins to turn...

00:23:51.990 --> 00:24:02.540
And even on days when the morning doesn’t come, it shines a light in my heart.

00:24:05.530 --> 00:24:08.640
If it means defeating Kazuma,
I don't mind sacrificing my life!

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:11.560
Ahahahahaha! Ha ha ha, ha...

00:24:11.560 --> 00:24:13.680
Kai, can't you give it a rest?

00:24:13.680 --> 00:24:15.350
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan:

00:24:15.350 --> 00:24:18.460
I Hate Things that Turn!!
Kai and Monica's Three-Legged Race!

00:24:18.460 --> 00:24:19.500
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.290 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate Seeds of Knowledge!!

00:24:22.730 --> 00:24:25.850
Green onions have a recovery effect on chilled bodies.

00:24:25.850 --> 00:24:28.000
When your body gets cold, bathe in a mixture of green onions, miso, and ginger.

00:24:28.000 --> 00:24:31.080
Apply heat, and your body will warm up and feel wonderful!

00:24:31.080 --> 00:24:31.750
Onion on I!

00:24:32.160 --> 00:24:33.950
Ehhh!?!
